  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。架空の人物、事例、製品を使った文章であり、実在の制度・調査結果・個別の医療栄養助言ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "A student named Rina writes a short English essay about school uniforms.",
          "ja": "リナという生徒は制服についての短い英作文を書く。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She lists several advantages and disadvantages and checks the spelling of her words.",
          "ja": "利点と欠点をいくつか列挙し語の綴りを確認する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Although each sentence is understandable, her teacher finds the overall argument difficult to follow.",
          "ja": "各文は理解できるが教師は全体の議論を追いにくいと感じる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The teacher asks Rina to examine the relationships between her sentences.",
          "ja": "教師は文同士の関係を調べるようリナに頼む。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Rina notices that two neighboring sentences describe opposing ideas.",
          "ja": "隣り合う二文が対立する考えを記述するとリナは気づく。"
        },
        {
          "en": "One explains that uniforms may reduce differences in appearance, and the next describes a limitation of that idea.",
          "ja": "一文は制服が外見の違いを減らし得ると説明し次はその考えの限界を述べる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She adds a connecting expression to make the contrast clearer.",
          "ja": "対比をより明確にするため接続表現を加える。"
        },
        {
          "en": "In another paragraph, she uses an expression indicating that an example supports the preceding statement.",
          "ja": "別段落では例が前の記述を支持することを示す表現を使う。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "However, the teacher warns her that adding more connecting words will not automatically improve every essay.",
          "ja": "しかし接続語を増やしても全作文が自動的に改善するわけではないと教師は注意する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A word suggesting a contrast cannot create a genuine contrast between unrelated sentences.",
          "ja": "対比を示す語は無関係な文間に本物の対比を作れない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Rina therefore checks whether the relationships she wants to express are actually supported by the content.",
          "ja": "そこで表したい関係が実際に内容で支えられるか確認する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Sometimes she changes a sentence rather than simply inserting another expression.",
          "ja": "時に別表現を単に挿入せず文を変更する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The revised essay is easier to understand because its organization has become clearer.",
          "ja": "構成がより明確になったため修正作文は理解しやすい。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Rina asks a classmate to identify the main claim and the reasons supporting it.",
          "ja": "級友に主張とそれを支持する理由を特定するよう頼む。"
        },
        {
          "en": "His response helps her discover a place where an additional explanation is needed.",
          "ja": "返答は追加説明が必要な箇所を発見する助けになる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She learns to consider how a reader moves from one idea to the next.",
          "ja": "読者が一つの考えから次へどう移るか考えることを学ぶ。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Good writing involves more than producing correct individual sentences.",
          "ja": "良い作文には正しい個々の文を作る以上のことが関わる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It also depends on arranging ideas so that their relationships are understandable.",
          "ja": "関係が理解できるよう考えを配置することにも依存する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Connecting expressions help readers recognize these relationships, but they cannot replace careful reasoning.",
          "ja": "接続表現は関係の認識を助けるが慎重な推論の代わりにはならない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "For Rina, a small word becomes a useful reminder of the larger structure of her writing.",
          "ja": "リナにとって小さな語が作文のより大きな構造を思い出させる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
